Origin (azsupport/ports): openSUSE zip 3.0 (Tumbleweed), zip-3.0-nomutilation.patch
 (tbehrens@suse.com, 03.04.2014), the names of the file made those of zip.c. With -j
 (no paths) add_filter() cut the path off each pattern of -i, -x and -R (in2ex() and
 ex2in() with pathput 0): zip -j a.zip dir/a.txt dir/sub/c.txt -x 'dir/sub/*' excluded
 every file ("Nothing to do!"), -i 'dir/sub/*' included every file. The patterns are
 added with the paths kept. Tested on Linux with the patches of the official port:
 both as expected with it, as above without.

